acme-sre: Hey team — since the latest rollout our TypeScript generation is dropping a bunch of interface fields and comments. Our CI started failing with tsc errors. Example input prompt we send:

acme-sre: ```prompt
# generate TypeScript interface from JSON schema
{
  "name": "User",
  "properties": {
    "id": { "type": "string" },
    "email": { "type": "string", "format": "email" },
    "profile": { "type": "object", "properties": { "bio": { "type": "string" }, "avatarUrl": { "type": "string" } } }
  }
}
```

acme-sre: Expected output (compiled OK):

acme-sre: ```ts
export interface User {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  profile?: {
    bio?: string;
    avatarUrl?: string;
  };
}
```

acme-sre: Actual output we get from the API after rollout: interface truncated (missing profile.avatarUrl and missing optional markers), plus inline comments stripped: 

acme-sre: ```ts
export interface User {
  id: string
  email: string
  profile: {
    bio: string
  }
}
```

acme-sre: tsc error: Property 'avatarUrl' does not exist on type 'User'. Also style change: no semicolons and non-optional profile now required which breaks our callers.

Maya: Sorry about the regression — can you share the request_id(s) and the model/version you called? Also the full curl you used if possible.

acme-sre: request_id: rq_0a1b2c3d, called model: redwood-code-1.0.0 (we saw the rollout message around 2169999950). curl:

acme-sre: ```bash
curl -s -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate \n -H 'Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN' \n -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \n -d '{"model":"redwood-code-1.0.0","prompt":"<schema>","temperature":0.2,"stop":"\n\n" }'
```

Josh: Thanks, adding eng-runtime. Quick question — are you using the codegen pipeline with the new description-to-ts template or the generic text generation path? Any caching/proxy between you and the API?

acme-sre: We call the /generate endpoint with content-type application/json, no proxy. We use the codegen pipeline (synthesize-ts). Verified by toggling to an older model (redwood-code-0.9.7) — CI passes.

deploy-bot: Canary rollout for redwood-code-1.0.0 completed at 2169999950 :white_check_mark:

Liam: Noted. Initial look: the new release includes a short decoding tweak that can favor shorter completions under certain stop-token/emission combos. That could explain field truncation and removed trailing semicolons/comments. Can you reproduce locally with the same seed/stop? I'll try to reproduce with the exact request_id.

acme-sre: Repro steps we used in CI:

acme-sre: 1) POST same curl above
2) run tsc
3) fail on missing property

Maya: I'm escalating this to a P1 ticket and pinging eng-runtime + eng-ml. @Josh @Liam can you take a look at decoding/stop/tokenization differences between 0.9.7 and 1.0.0? Customer is blocked in CI. :exclamation:

Josh: ACK, will diff logits/beam traces and run A/B with stop tokens. If confirmed, we can hotfix the decoding policy or revert the rollout.

Liam: I'll run a narrow bisect on the model serving changes and try to reproduce deterministically. If it's a truncation bias, we can patch the stopping criteria or adjust min_tokens.

Maya: Thanks — will keep the customer posted. acme-sre, I'll follow up with an internal ticket ID and a short-term mitigation (pin model to 0.9.7) until we have a fix. :pray:

acme-sre: Appreciate it. Please include any temporary sanitizer we can run on generated code to avoid CI failures (e.g., check for missing properties) while you investigate.
